1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,550
Hi Jeannie. How's it going?

2
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:04,280
Oh, hello Dan. Pretty well, thanks

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:07,200
Have you managed to get the money for the course yet?

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,960
Yes, that's all sorted out now, thanks. It took long enough, though.

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:16,329
It was practically a year ago that I applied to my local council for a grant,

6
00:00:16,329 --> 00:00:19,060
and it took them six months to turn me down.

7
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,940
That's really slow.

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:25,960
And I thought I was eligible for government funding, but it seems I was mistaken.

9
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:31,407
So then I asked the boss of the company I used to work for if they would sponsor me,

10
00:00:31,407 --> 00:00:34,560
and much to my surprise, he said they'd make a contribution.

11
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:38,000
But what about college grants and scholarships

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,260
There must be some you could apply for.

13
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,300
Yes, there are, but they're all

14
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,640
so small that I decided to leave them until I was desperate.

15
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,200
Uhuh.

16
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,620
And in fact I didn't need to apply.

17
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:52,220
My parents had been saying that as I already had a job

18
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,530
I ought to support myself through college.

19
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:59,400
But in the end they took pity on me, so now I've just about got enough.

20
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,350
That's good.

21
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:07,410
So now I can put a bit of effort into meeting people - I haven't had time so far. Any suggestions?

22
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:10,430
What about joining some college clubs?

23
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:12,900
Oh right. You joined several didn't you?

24
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:17,504
Yes, I'm in the drama club. It's our first performance next week,

25
00:01:17,504 --> 00:01:23,260
so we're rehearsing frantically, and I've got behind with my work, but it's worth it.

26
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:26,420
I'm hoping to be in the spring production, too.

27
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:29,830
I've never liked acting. Are you doing anything else?

28
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:34,820
I enjoyed singing when I was at school, so I joined a group when I came to college.

29
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:37,980
I don't think the conductor stretches us enough, though

30
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:40,220
so I'll give up after the next concert.

31
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:42,885
And I also joined the debating society.

32
00:01:42,885 --> 00:01:46,800
It's fun, but with all the rehearsing I'm doing

33
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:50,120
something has to go, and I'm afraid that's the one.

34
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,730
Do you do any sports?

35
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:54,240
Yes, I'm in one of the hockey teams

36
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,700
I'm not very good, but I'd really miss it if I stopped.

37
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,900
I decided to try tennis when I came to college

38
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,789
and I'm finding it pretty tough going.

39
00:02:03,789 --> 00:02:05,580
I'm simply not fit enough.

40
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:08,010
Nor me. I think I'll give that a miss!

41
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:13,080
I'm hoping it'll help me to build up my stamina, but it'll probably be a long haul.

42
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:13,730
Good luck.

43
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:14,500
Thanks.

44
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:16,320
How are you finding the course?

45
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:19,000
I wish we had more seminars.

46
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,610
What? I'd have thought we had more than enough already.

47
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:27,521
All those people saying clever things that I could never think of- it's quite interesting,

48
00:02:27,521 --> 00:02:31,450
but I wonder if I'm clever enough to be doing this course.

49
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:34,210
I find it helpful to listen to the other people.

50
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:37,220
I like the way we're exploring the subject

51
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:39,950
and working towards getting insight into it.

52
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:42,364
How do you get on with your tutor?

53
00:02:42,364 --> 00:02:45,480
I don't think I'm on the same wavelength as mine

54
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:48,700
so I feel I'm not getting anything out of the tutorials.

55
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:51,700
It would be more productive to read a book instead.

56
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:56,640
Oh, mine's very demanding. She gives me lots of feedback and advice

57
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:59,150
so I've got much better at writing essays.

58
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:02,940
And she's helping me plan my revision for the end-of-year exams.

59
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,270
Do tell me, I always struggle with revision.

60
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:11,840
Well, the first thing is to find out exactly what's required in the exams.

61
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:15,420
Mm. Would it help to get hold of some past papers?

62
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:17,950
Yes. They'll help to make it clear.

63
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:20,280
Right, I'll do that. Then what?

64
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:23,040
Then you can sort out your revision priorities

65
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,250
based on what's most likely to come up.

66
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:28,360
I put these on a card, and read them through regularly.

67
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:28,920
Uhuh.

68
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:30,730
But that isn't enough in itself.

69
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:32,980
You also need a timetable

70
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:35,860
to see how you can fit everything in, in the time available.

71
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,800
Then keep it in front of you while you're studying.

72
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:41,500
I've done that before, but it hasn't helped me!

73
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,580
Maybe you need to do something different every day

74
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:47,488
so if you break down your revision into small tasks,

75
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:51,270
and allocate them to specific days, there's more incentive to tackle them.

76
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:54,800
With big topics you're more likely to put off starting.

77
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,060
Good idea.

78
00:03:56,060 --> 00:04:00,234
And as I revise each topic I write a single paragraph about it -

79
00:04:00,234 --> 00:04:05,050
then later can read it through quickly, and it helps fix things in my mind.

80
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:06,200
That's brilliant.

81
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:09,640
I also write answers to questions for the exam practice

82
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,780
It's hard to make myself do it, though!

83
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:16,820
Well, I'll try. Thanks a lot, Jeannie. That's a great help.

84
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:17,600
No problem.

85
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,700
See you around.

86
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:19,500
Bye.
